StructuredTest
├── toAmount
│   ├── given a finite number
│   │   └── it is taken as is
│   ├── given a number that is not finite
│   │   └── it is rejected
│   ├── given a machine-normalised string
│   │   ├── it parses it
│   │   └── it strips grouping separators
│   ├── given a string that is not a number
│   │   └── it is rejected
│   └── given anything else
│       └── it is rejected
├── readStructuredPrices
│   ├── given JSON-LD
│   │   ├── it reads a Product/Offer block
│   │   ├── it walks @graph and arrays
│   │   ├── it reads both ends of an AggregateOffer
│   │   ├── given a block is malformed
│   │   │   └── it survives without losing the good ones
│   │   ├── given a block is larger than the parse cap
│   │   │   └── it skips that block
│   │   ├── given a block is empty
│   │   │   └── it skips that block
│   │   ├── given the price is a number rather than a string
│   │   │   └── it reads it
│   │   ├── given the price is not finite
│   │   │   └── it ignores the block
│   │   ├── given the price is not a number at all
│   │   │   └── it ignores the block
│   │   └── given there is no currency
│   │       └── it ignores the block — an amount alone is not a price
│   ├── given microdata
│   │   ├── it reads the content attribute
│   │   ├── given there is no content attribute
│   │   │   └── it reads the visible text
│   │   ├── given the amount is not readable
│   │   │   └── it skips the element
│   │   ├── given the amount is zero or negative
│   │   │   └── it skips the element
│   │   ├── given the currency is stated as text rather than an attribute
│   │   │   └── it reads the text
│   │   ├── given there is no currency in scope
│   │   │   └── it skips the element
│   │   └── given the price sits outside any itemscope
│   │       └── it looks for the currency across the whole root
│   └── given OpenGraph tags
│       ├── it reads the price
│       ├── given the amount tag is missing
│       │   └── it reads nothing
│       └── given the currency tag is missing
│           └── it reads nothing
├── documentCurrency
│   ├── given the page agrees on one currency
│   │   └── it reports that currency
│   ├── given the page is multi-currency
│   │   └── it reports nothing
│   └── given the page states no price at all
│       └── it reports nothing
├── digitProjection
│   ├── it keeps only the digits
│   └── given text with no digits
│       └── it returns nothing
├── projectionsFor
│   ├── it covers the renderings a price actually takes
│   └── given a whole number
│       └── it covers the two-decimal rendering as well
├── locatePrices
│   ├── given no structured prices
│   │   └── it returns nothing
│   ├── given a price split across spans
│   │   └── it finds the element regex reads as 4999
│   ├── given several matching elements
│   │   └── it prefers the smallest
│   ├── given the amount is nowhere on screen
│   │   └── it returns nothing
│   ├── given two prices with the same digits
│   │   └── it does not give them the same element
│   ├── given an element holds no digits
│   │   └── it is not a candidate
│   ├── given an element holds digits that do not match
│   │   └── it is not chosen
│   └── given a Shopify cents-integer
│       ├── given the screen shows two decimals
│       │   └── it reads the value as cents
│       └── given the screen shows the integer itself
│           └── it keeps the integer
└── the oracle beats regex where regex is weakest
    ├── it fixes the currency for the whole page
    └── it reads a price regex would get 100x wrong
